  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Tailwind Setup**\n\nI\'m making good progress! I\'ve been thinking about the new features in Tailwind v4 and am planning to define the color variables, font families, utility helpers, and base styles directly within `src/index.css`. I\'m also ensuring the `index.html` file properly loads the Google Fonts, including `Plus Jakarta Sans`, `Space Grotesk`, and `Material Symbols Outlined`.\n\n\n**Analyzing Image Usage**\n\nI\'m now focused on image handling. I\'ve noted the available image files and how they are referenced in the HTML, specifically the hotlinking through Google\'s public URLs. I\'ve documented the URLs for the header logo, profile picture and court images, so I can start integrating them.\n\n\n**Integrating Image Assets**\n\nI\'m now integrating the image assets. I\'ve successfully incorporated the image URLs for the central panorama, indoor court, open-air court, and hero match court images into the project. My next step will be to make the images dynamic to improve the experience of the overall project.\n\n\n**Incorporating Player Profiles**\n\nI\'ve just added player profile images for Card 2. I\'ve successfully incorporated URLs for three players, and will proceed to integrate these images into the correct card elements. I\'m focusing on ensuring these images render properly and dynamically as intended.\n\n\n**Adding Club Amenities**\n\nI\'ve just added URLs for the reservation miniature, and club amenity images for Canchas Cristal and Quincho & 3er Tiempo. I\'m moving toward integrating these image assets into the corresponding elements within the project. The next step is to test their display and responsiveness.\n\n\n\n**Planning Project Structure**\n\nI\'m now outlining the project\'s structure. I\'ve decided on `metadata.json` for name and description: \"Padel Assist Pro,\" describing it as \"Padel court booking, real-time match management, voucher validation, and court management panel\". I\'m also planning to update `index.html` with relevant title, description, and `og` tags. I\'ll need to define how to handle the new court location images.\n\n\n**Defining Type Structures**\n\nI\'m now creating essential types within `src/types.ts`. I\'ve outlined `UserRole`, `UserProfile`, `Court`, `Amenity`, `BookingStatus`, `Booking`, and `TimeSlot` structures, covering crucial data fields. These structures lay the groundwork for a robust application data model. I\'m focusing on accuracy and anticipating potential future additions to these definitions.\n\n\n**Outlining API Service**\n\nI\'m now detailing `src/apiService.ts` functionalities. I\'ve listed various functions for data fetching (`fetchCourts`, `fetchAmenities`, etc.), booking management (`createBooking`, `cancelBooking`), payment handling (`uploadPaymentProof`, `confirmPaymentByCanchero`), and court slot manipulation (`blockCourtSlot`). I\'m also considering advanced features like `autoSlotQuickMatch`, `joinOpenMatch`, and user profile updates. Furthermore, I\'ve outlined login as admin, password reset handling and a potential AI powered feature, `generateAndAssignAIRoutine`. Lastly, I\'m working to integrate court, time and navigation types.\n\n\n**Designing UI Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on UI components, starting with `AppHeader.tsx`. I\'m planning the \"Padel Assist\" logo, \"Pro\" badge, and the live status display. I also need to incorporate the profile avatar button, complete with the dropdown or modal for profile switching and data resets. I\'m also planning the bottom navigation tabs, the matchmaking banner, court cards, a quick match drawer, and a calendar strip.\n\n\n**Developing UI Components**\n\nI\'m now detailing the UI components. I\'m focusing on new components, including `TimeSlotGrid.tsx`, covering morning, afternoon, and night slots. I\'m also planning `BookingSummarySheet.tsx`, a bottom sheet for booking previews, payment with a breakdown, and a team note input. I\'m also planning the `PaymentDrawer.tsx`, with bank transfer details and upload features. The CancelModal, CancheroPanel and ClubRulesAccordion are also in design.\n\n\n**Planning Match Details**\n\nI\'m now detailing the match detail modal, and also the toast notifications needed to provide dynamic feedback to the user on several actions. I\'m focusing on providing details of confirmed matches, including players, court info and invoice. Also, I need toast notifications with user friendly messages, such as confirmation messages.\n\n\n\n"
