  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the SQL Function**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `getAvailableSlotsFromDb` function within `src/apiService.ts`. I\'m focusing on defining the PL/pgSQL function. The function will take a court ID, a date, and an optional slot duration, returning available slot start times. The SQL function will return a table with the start times.\n\n\n**Refining the SQL Logic**\n\nI\'ve refined the core SQL logic. I\'ve focused on ensuring the `getAvailableSlotsFromDb` PL/pgSQL function correctly iterates through potential slots, starting from the club\'s opening time and continuing until closing. The query now generates a series of `TIMESTAMPTZ` values.\n\n\n**Implementing the TS Function**\n\nI\'m now integrating the SQL function within the TypeScript environment. I\'m building out `getAvailableSlots` to call the SQL function. I\'m ensuring it accounts for club hours (07:00 to 23:00) and filters out slots overlapping with confirmed or pending bookings.\n\n\n**Evaluating Time Slot Conflicts**\n\nI\'m now evaluating potential slot conflicts. I\'m calculating and tracking the current start and end times in minutes. I\'m now checking for overlap with existing bookings. I\'m focusing on handling both date matching and specifically checking the demo data for specific date overlaps.\n\n\n**Analyzing Slot Availability**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the slot availability logic. I\'ve built up the structure for how to classify slots and determined how to resolve conflicts and categorize the slots into morning, afternoon, and night categories. I\'m focusing on the logic to categorize the time slots into morning, afternoon, and night based on the start time in minutes, and tagging some slots for special cases such as \"Fresca\" at 8:00 AM, \"Sin sol\" at 4:30 PM, or \"\303\232ltimo\" for the last night slot.\n\n\n"
