  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **Core Request**: Build \"Padel Assist Pro\", a high-performance padel club booking and management web app based on 4 provided mockup screens/HTMLs (`Canchas`, `Reservar`, `Partidos`, `Club/Modo Canchero`), integrating PostgreSQL DDL/RLS security policies and stored procedure `get_available_slots`, PWA installability, and recently requested `BookingCalendar.tsx` (`BookingGrid`) component with touch-optimized chips and WhatsApp deep link reporting.\n- **Architectural Rules**:\n  - `App.tsx`: Pure router & global state coordinator. No API or business logic here.\n  - `src/apiService.ts`: All business logic, mutations, DB operations, and Gemini Coach IA routines.\n  - `src/components/`: Reusable, focused components.\n  - `src/screens/`: High-level screen containers.\n  - `src/types.ts`: Central TypeScript interfaces.\n- **RLS & Security Rules**:\n  - `profiles`: Users view/edit only their own profile (`auth.uid() = id`).\n  - `courts` / `amenities`: Public read (`is_active = true`, `is_available = true`).\n  - `bookings`: Customers view only their own bookings; public availability grids anonymize reserved slots as \"Reservado\" or \"En juego\" without exposing names or phones.\n  - `club_admin`: Supervises all club bookings, desk payments, and blocks.\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Database & RLS Schema**:\n  - `src/db/schema.sql`: Contains full PostgreSQL DDL (`profiles`, `courts`, `amenities_catalog`, `bookings`), RLS policies, and `get_available_slots` PL/pgSQL function.\n- **PWA Integration**:\n  - Dependencies: Installed `vite-plugin-pwa` and `@supabase/supabase-js`.\n  - Manifest & Assets: `public/manifest.json` configured with name \"Padel Assist\", short_name \"PadelAssist\", theme color `#10b981`, background `#09090b`. Generated valid PNGs (`icon-192.png`, `icon-512.png`, `apple-touch-icon.png`) and `public/icon.svg`.\n  - Configs: `vite.config.ts` has `VitePWA` with autoUpdate and `devOptions: { enabled: true }`. `tsconfig.json` has `\"types\": [\"vite/client\", \"vite-plugin-pwa/client\"]`. `index.html` has PWA meta tags and manifest links.\n  - Components: `src/hooks/usePWAInstall.ts`, `src/components/PWAInstallButton.tsx` (mounted in `AppHeader` and `ClubScreen`), and `src/components/OfflineIndicator.tsx` (mounted in `App.tsx`).\n- **Core App & Screens**:\n  - `src/screens/CanchasScreen.tsx`: Court cards, filters, 4th player matchmaking banner, quick auto-slot.\n  - `src/screens/ReservarScreen.tsx`: Weekly calendar horizon carousel, court selector, duration switcher (60, 90, 120 min), dynamic slot grid driven by `getAvailableSlots`, and Step 1/2 summary sheet.\n  - `src/screens/PartidosScreen.tsx`: Upcoming, completed, and cancelled tabs; hero match with countdown & upload proof button; confirmed match with player alignment; `PaymentDrawer` and `CancelModal`.\n  - `src/screens/ClubScreen.tsx`: Toggle between \"Vista Jugador\" (club info, location, rules accordions, amenities, persistent WhatsApp reception button) and \"Modo Canchero\" (`CancheroPanel` with swipe-to-confirm payment, call/WhatsApp, and blocking modal).\n- **Recent Additions**:\n  - Created `src/supabaseClient.ts` with safe environment fallback.\n  - Created `src/components/BookingCalendar.tsx` exporting `BookingGrid` and `BookingCalendar` with touch-optimized chips, native date picker + quick chips (Hoy, Ma\303\261ana), and WhatsApp deep link confirmation.\n  - Added `.env.example` placeholders for `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` and `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`.\n\n### 3. Key Findings & Decisions\n- `get_available_slots`: Replicated in `src/apiService.ts` via `getAvailableSlots(courtId, dateStr, durationMinutes)` running from 07:00 to 23:00, checking overlap against confirmed/pending bookings.\n- `BookingGrid` handles both live Supabase RPC and local state fallback so that the app remains 100% interactive and functional even before real Supabase keys are provided.\n- Compilation and linting both passed cleanly with 0 errors (`tsc --noEmit`).\n\n### 4. Active Context\n- File `src/components/BookingCalendar.tsx` is created.\n- In progress: Integrating `BookingGrid` into `src/screens/ReservarScreen.tsx` as a complementary view mode (e.g., toggle between \"Vista Agenda Completa\" and \"Selector R\303\241pido Chips\") so the user can interact with both the design mockup layout and the new touch-optimized chip selector.\n\n### 5. Next Steps\n1. **Update `src/screens/ReservarScreen.tsx`**:\n   - Add a subtle toggle tab at the top of `ReservarScreen` (e.g., \"Agenda Detallada\" vs \"Selector R\303\241pido Chips\") to render `BookingGrid` directly or integrate it cleanly into the booking flow.\n   - When a booking is made via `BookingGrid`, notify `onBookingConfirmed` or refresh the `mis-partidos` screen.\n2. **Run verification**:\n   - Execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` to confirm the final build state.\n3. **Notify User**:\n   - Deliver a concise summary confirming `BookingCalendar.tsx` / `BookingGrid` implementation, touch-optimized chips, and WhatsApp receipt reporting.\n\n### 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- Must maintain strict file architecture: no business logic in `App.tsx`.\n- Must keep exact branding and styles (`#0f131c`, `#10b981`, `#4edea3`, Plus Jakarta Sans / Space Grotesk).\n- WhatsApp deep link must format text with the booked slot time.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_end: 202
    user_requests: "Here is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.3.3\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^6.1.1\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^8.3.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\n@types/react: ^19.3.0\n@types/react-dom: ^19.3.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.3.3\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ^7.0.2\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(<App />);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  },\n  \"exclude\": [\"dist\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\342\200\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    user_requests: "Build me an app with screens that look like this. You can hotlink images from the html -- 1. Perfiles de usuario (complemento de auth.users)\nCREATE TYPE user_role AS ENUM (\'customer\', \'club_admin\', \'superadmin\');\n\nCREATE TABLE profiles (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    full_name TEXT NOT NULL,\n    phone TEXT NOT NULL,\n    avatar_url TEXT,\n    role user_role DEFAULT \'customer\',\n    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()\n);\n\n-- 2. Canchas e infraestructura\nCREATE TABLE courts (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n    name TEXT NOT NULL, -- ej: \"Cancha 1 (Panor\303\241mica)\"\n    type TEXT NOT NULL, -- \"Cristal Techada\", \"Malla Descubierta\"\n    is_active BOOLEAN DEFAULT TRUE,\n    hourly_rate NUMERIC(10, 2) NOT NULL,\n    photos TEXT[] DEFAULT \'{}\',\n    description TEXT,\n    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()\n);\n\n-- 3. Cat\303\241logo de servicios adicionales (Cafeter\303\255a, Alquiler de palas, Tienda)\nCREATE TABLE amenities_catalog (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n    title TEXT NOT NULL, -- ej: \"Pala Bullpadel Pro\", \"Gatorade 500ml\", \"Duchas y Vestuarios\"\n    category TEXT NOT NULL, -- \'alquiler\', \'tienda\', \'servicio_gratis\'\n    price NUMERIC(10, 2) DEFAULT 0.00,\n    is_available BOOLEAN DEFAULT TRUE,\n    image_url TEXT\n);\n\n-- 4. Reservas de Canchas\nCREATE TYPE booking_status AS ENUM (\'pending_payment\', \'confirmed\', \'cancelled\', \'completed\');\n\nCREATE TABLE bookings (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n    court_id UUID REFERENCES courts(id) ON DELETE RESTRICT,\n    user_id UUID REFERENCES profiles(id) ON DELETE SET NULL,\n    guest_name TEXT, -- Por si el club la anota manualmente para alguien sin app\n    guest_phone TEXT,\n    start_time TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,\n    end_time TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,\n    total_price NUMERIC(10, 2) NOT NULL,\n    status booking_status DEFAULT \'pending_payment\',\n    payment_proof_url TEXT,\n    notes TEXT,\n    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW(),\n    \n    -- Evita solapamiento de horarios exactos en la misma cancha\n    CONSTRAINT check_booking_duration CHECK (end_time > start_time)\n);\n\n-- \303\215ndice para acelerar la consulta de disponibilidad horaria\nCREATE INDEX idx_bookings_court_time ON bookings (court_id, start_time, end_time);\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nMedia attachment: User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/Image_1_548e76c8.png (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/Image_1_548e76c8.png). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/Image_1_548e76c8.png. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\n  User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/Image_2_8c1b8345.html (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/Image_2_8c1b8345.html). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/Image_2_8c1b8345.html. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\n  User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/Image_3_c68bf17a.png (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/Image_3_c68bf17a.png). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/Image_3_c68bf17a.png. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\n  User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/Image_4_b1c76ef9.html (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/Image_4_b1c76ef9.html). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/Image_4_b1c76ef9.html. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\n  User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/Image_5_7551111e.png (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/Image_5_7551111e.png). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/Image_5_7551111e.png. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\n  User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/Image_6_d5f3bdf9.html (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/Image_6_d5f3bdf9.html). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/Image_6_d5f3bdf9.html. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\n  User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/Image_7_b113a785.png (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/Image_7_b113a785.png). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/Image_7_b113a785.png. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\n  User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/Image_8_30db60e2.html (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/Image_8_30db60e2.html). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/Image_8_30db60e2.html. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    user_requests: "-- Habilitar RLS en tablas cr\303\255ticas\nALTER TABLE profiles ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;\nALTER TABLE bookings ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;\nALTER TABLE courts ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;\nALTER TABLE amenities_catalog ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;\n\n-- REGLAS PROFILES:\n-- Cada usuario solo edita y lee su perfil; el administrador del club ve los perfiles de sus clientes\nCREATE POLICY \"Users can view own profile\" \nON profiles FOR SELECT USING (auth.uid() = id);\n\nCREATE POLICY \"Users can update own profile\" \nON profiles FOR UPDATE USING (auth.uid() = id);\n\n-- REGLAS COURTS & CATALOG:\n-- Cualquiera (incluso sin login) puede ver canchas y cat\303\241logo para incentivar la visita\nCREATE POLICY \"Public read courts\" \nON courts FOR SELECT USING (is_active = TRUE);\n\nCREATE POLICY \"Public read amenities\" \nON amenities_catalog FOR SELECT USING (is_available = TRUE);\n\n-- REGLAS BOOKINGS (Crucial para privacidad):\n-- Los clientes solo ven el horario bloqueado en la vista p\303\272blica, pero NO los datos de qui\303\251n reserv\303\263\nCREATE POLICY \"Customers view own booking details\" \nON bookings FOR SELECT \nUSING (\n    auth.uid() = user_id \n    OR \n    EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM profiles WHERE profiles.id = auth.uid() AND profiles.role = \'club_admin\')\n);\n\n-- Inserci\303\263n de reserva: Usuarios autenticados\nCREATE POLICY \"Authenticated users can create bookings\" \nON bookings FOR INSERT \nWITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);"
    user_requests: "CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION get_available_slots(\n    p_court_id UUID,\n    p_date DATE,\n    p_slot_duration_minutes INT DEFAULT 90\n)\nRETURNS TABLE (slot_start TIMESTAMPTZ, slot_end TIMESTAMPTZ, is_available BOOLEAN) \nLANGUAGE plpgsql\nSECURITY DEFINER\nAS $$\nDECLARE\n    club_open TIME := \'07:00:00\';\n    club_close TIME := \'23:00:00\';\n    curr_slot_start TIMESTAMPTZ;\n    curr_slot_end TIMESTAMPTZ;\nBEGIN\n    curr_slot_start := (p_date + club_open)::TIMESTAMPTZ;\n    \n    WHILE (curr_slot_start + (p_slot_duration_minutes || \' minutes\')::INTERVAL) <= (p_date + club_close)::TIMESTAMPTZ LOOP\n        curr_slot_end := curr_slot_start + (p_slot_duration_minutes || \' minutes\')::INTERVAL;\n        \n        RETURN QUERY\n        SELECT \n            curr_slot_start,\n            curr_slot_end,\n            NOT EXISTS (\n                SELECT 1 FROM bookings b\n                WHERE b.court_id = p_court_id\n                  AND b.status IN (\'confirmed\', \'pending_payment\')\n                  AND (b.start_time < curr_slot_end AND b.end_time > curr_slot_start)\n            );\n            \n        curr_slot_start := curr_slot_end;\n    END LOOP;\nEND;\n$$;"
    user_requests: "4. Frontend: Experiencia M\303\263vil de Alto Rendimiento\nPara que cargue instant\303\241neamente y sea instalable como app web en Android/iPhone sin costo de tienda:  {\n  \"name\": \"Padel Assist\",\n  \"short_name\": \"PadelAssist\",\n  \"start_url\": \"/\",\n  \"display\": \"standalone\",\n  \"background_color\": \"#09090b\",\n  \"theme_color\": \"#10b981\",\n  \"icons\": [\n    {\n      \"src\": \"/icon-192.png\",\n      \"sizes\": \"192x192\",\n      \"type\": \"image/png\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"src\": \"/icon-512.png\",\n      \"sizes\": \"512x512\",\n      \"type\": \"image/png\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
    user_requests: "Componente de Reserva y Visualizaci\303\263n (BookingCalendar.tsx)\nFlujo optimizado para pantallas t\303\241ctiles con selector de turnos estilo chips:import React, { useState, useEffect } from \'react\';\nimport { createClient } from \'@supabase/supabase-js\';\n\nconst supabase = createClient(\'https://TU_PROYECTO.supabase.co\', \'TU_ANON_KEY\');\n\nexport const BookingGrid = ({ courtId }: { courtId: string }) => {\n  const [selectedDate, setSelectedDate] = useState(new Date().toISOString().split(\'T\')[0]);\n  const [slots, setSlots] = useState<any[]>([]);\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    fetchSlots();\n  }, [courtId, selectedDate]);\n\n  const fetchSlots = async () => {\n    setLoading(true);\n    const { data, error } = await supabase.rpc(\'get_available_slots\', {\n      p_court_id: courtId,\n      p_date: selectedDate,\n      p_slot_duration_minutes: 90\n    });\n    if (!error && data) setSlots(data);\n    setLoading(false);\n  };\n\n  const handleBooking = async (slot: any) => {\n    const { data: { user } } = await supabase.auth.getUser();\n    if (!user) {\n      alert(\"Por favor inicia sesi\303\263n con tu n\303\272mero para reservar.\");\n      return;\n    }\n\n    const { error } = await supabase.from(\'bookings\').insert({\n      court_id: courtId,\n      user_id: user.id,\n      start_time: slot.slot_start,\n      end_time: slot.slot_end,\n      total_price: 35.00, // Ajustar seg\303\272n tarifa de cancha\n      status: \'pending_payment\'\n    });\n\n    if (!error) {\n      // Disparar mensaje con deep link a WhatsApp para reportar comprobante\n      const text = encodeURIComponent(`Hola! Acabo de reservar en Padel Assist para el horario ${new Date(slot.slot_start).toLocaleTimeString([], {hour: \'2-digit\', minute:\'2-digit\'})}. Adjunto comprobante.`);\n      window.open(`https://wa.me/573001234567?text=${text}`, \'_blank\');\n      fetchSlots();\n    }\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"p-4 max-w-md mx-auto bg-zinc-950 text-white rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800\">\n      <div className=\"flex items-center justify-between mb-4\">\n        <h2 className=\"text-lg font-bold text-emerald-400\">Selecciona tu turno</h2>\n        <input \n          type=\"date\" \n          value={selectedDate} \n          onChange={(e) => setSelectedDate(e.target.value)}\n          className=\"bg-zinc-800 text-sm p-2 rounded-lg border border-zinc-700 text-white\"\n        />\n      </div>\n\n      {loading ? (\n        <div className=\"text-center py-8 text-zinc-400 text-sm\">Verificando canchas...</div>\n      ) : (\n        <div className=\"grid grid-cols-2 gap-2.5\">\n          {slots.map((s, idx) => {\n            const timeStr = `${new Date(s.slot_start).toLocaleTimeString([], {hour: \'2-digit\', minute:\'2-digit\'})} - ${new Date(s.slot_end).toLocaleTimeString([], {hour: \'2-digit\', minute:\'2-digit\'})}`;\n            return (\n              <button\n                key={idx}\n                disabled={!s.is_available}\n                onClick={() => handleBooking(s)}\n                className={`py-3 px-2 rounded-xl text-xs font-semibold transition-all ${\n                  s.is_available \n                    ? \'bg-zinc-900 border border-emerald-500/40 text-emerald-300 hover:bg-emerald-600 hover:text-white\' \n                    : \'bg-zinc-900/40 border border-zinc-800 text-zinc-600 cursor-not-allowed line-through\'\n                }`}\n              >\n                {timeStr}\n              </button>\n            );\n          })}\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n};"
    render_latest_checkpoint: true
    total_subagent_count: 0
  }
}
