  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Component Structure**\n\nI\'m currently reviewing the component structure, specifically focusing on `src/App.tsx` and `src/screens/ReservarScreen.tsx`. I\'m paying close attention to how `ReservarScreen` is integrated within `App.tsx` using conditional rendering based on the `view` state. I\'m also examining the props passed to `ReservarScreen`, including `user`, `courts`, and `selectedCourtId`. My focus is on understanding the data flow and component relationships.\n\n\n**Refining Screen Mode Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how to integrate different views within `ReservarScreen.tsx`. I\'m exploring a sub-mode toggle at the top of the screen to switch between a \"Vista Agenda Detallada\" (calendar strip) and \"Selector R\303\241pido Chips\" (BookingGrid). Successful bookings in `BookingGrid` should trigger a call to `onBookingConfirmed` or similar. I\'m checking the requirements of `BookingGrid`, it seems to need a `courtId` and an `onBookingSuccess` handler.\n\n\n**Implementing Booking Confirmation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on handling booking confirmations within `ReservarScreen`. The `BookingGrid` component will record bookings using `createBookingInDb`. The focus now is on what should happen when `onBookingSuccess` fires. I\'m exploring an approach where it either triggers an `onBookingConfirmed` callback or updates the `App.tsx` state and redirects to `mis-partidos`. This seems like the most elegant approach, and this is where I am focused now.\n\n\n**Resolving Data Redundancy**\n\nI\'ve hit a snag: `BookingGrid` already handles database interaction via `createBookingInDb` when booking. Passing booking data to `onBookingConfirmed` to ALSO call `createBookingInDb` would cause duplicate entries! I\'m now examining the logic within `BookingCalendar.tsx`, specifically lines 74-131, to understand how it currently handles booking confirmation to avoid duplicated calls.\n\n\n**Investigating Success Callback**\n\nI\'m now examining how the `onBookingSuccess` callback from `BookingGrid` is handled. It seems the component is correctly managing database interaction and generating a WhatsApp message, but how does this notify the application to reflect the new booking? I\'m looking at the flow: `BookingGrid` calls `onBookingSuccess`, and from there I need to determine how the state updates or the user is redirected or informed. In `App.tsx`, `setBookings(getStoredBookings())` seems key. I\'m double-checking whether `App.tsx` passes a refresh callback.\n\n\n**Confirming Clean Integration**\n\nI\'m now very satisfied with how `onQuickBookingSuccess` can be neatly integrated. I\'ve confirmed that `App.tsx` *can* pass `onQuickBookingSuccess` to `ReservarScreen`. I\'m happy with how the booking success message, bookings refresh, and redirect all seamlessly link. I\'ll need to confirm that that the `setBookings` and `getStoredBookings` functions are working as expected after the booking is made and confirmed.\n\n\n**Examining New View Toggle**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the implementation of the new view toggle within `ReservarScreen.tsx`. I\'m checking the segmented control design, particularly the button functionality and how it affects the `viewMode` state. I\'m satisfied the look and feel align with the rest of the application. The goal is to ensure a smooth transition between the calendar strip and the BookingGrid.\n\n\n**Implementing View Mode Logic**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implementation of the `viewMode` toggle, specifically the logic for when `viewMode` is `\'chips\'`.  When selected, I need to display the court selector, the `BookingGrid`, and the real-time slot information badge.  When `\'agenda\'` is active, I must show the calendar strip, court selector, duration switcher, and time slot grid. I\'m focusing on ensuring the correct components render based on the state.\n\n\n\n"
